🎬 Internship Task 1: Storytelling Mini Documentary | Rhombix Technologies
As part of my Video Editing & Content Creation internship at Rhombix Technologies, I completed Task 1: a 2-minute storytelling mini documentary titled “The Last Watch Repair Shop in Town.”
📖 The story: A watchmaker who has spent forty years keeping time alive faces a quiet, struggling shop. Then one visitor with a broken family watch reminds him why the work still matters.
This task focused on:
✅ Clear narrative structure with a beginning, middle, and end
✅ Pacing that follows the emotion: slow and warm, then lonely, then hopeful
✅ Voiceover, stock footage, music, and sound design working together
✅ Smooth cuts, simple transitions, and a consistent color grade
✅ Matching the picture to the words so every line lands
🎞️ Format: 16:9, 2 minutes
